0339: SapphireGpu, SweetSurface: per-surface account of CPU access for cache maintenance (kern.sweet_gpu_flush, default 0)

Needs 0336. No change of behaviour unless switched on.

A submission cleans and invalidates (dc civac) all of every surface it names that its client has mapped,
and the Metal driver maps every surface it imports, so the window server's frame surface (4.9 MB) is
maintained at every submission, inside the ring's lock (measured: ~1.5 ms per submission, 8.64 s of 8.91 s
in GEM_SUBMIT over 15 minutes). The GPU alone writes that surface.

- SweetSurface gets cpuEpoch, cleanEpoch and invalEpoch. cpuEpoch moves at every CPU access the kernel is
  told of: IOSurfaceLock/Unlock traps, mapping or unmapping a GPU buffer over the surface, GEM_CPU_PREP and
  GEM_CPU_FINI, the kernel's own CPU copies. cleanEpoch/invalEpoch are cpuEpoch as read before the last
  full dc cvac / dc civac.
- kern.sweet_gpu_flush (read-write, boot-arg gpu_flush): 0 (default) unchanged; 1 a submission maintains a
  surface by that account: dc civac when it may write it (MSM_SUBMIT_BO_WRITE, or neither flag) and
  invalEpoch != cpuEpoch, dc cvac when it only reads it and cleanEpoch != cpuEpoch, nothing otherwise; the
  panel copy cleans by the same account; 2 as 1, and the client mapping of a surface's buffer is refused (a
  client then reaches the pixels through IOSurface and its locks only).
- kern.sweet_gpu_flush_stats (read only): surfaces named, skipped, cleaned, cleaned and invalidated (with
  bytes), mappings refused.

Mode 1 is complete only if no process accesses a surface through its GPU client mapping without locking
the surface; mode 2 makes such an access visible.

Locking: epochs are 32-bit words; cpuEpoch is only incremented atomically; clean/invalEpoch are stored
under service_lock or fPresentLock with the value read before the pass. Nothing new sleeps or spins.

Measured (one boot, n=1 per condition, home screen swipes): with kern.sweet_fb_queue=1, cache maintenance
per submission 1.63 ms with kern.sweet_gpu_flush=0 and 0.01 ms with 1; App Library and Control Center
render the same in screenshots.

